2. THE ARCHIVED CONTENT: not licensed, and not ours to license
---------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to `mirror/` and to the site content embedded in the distributed
applications: the HTML, images, Flash (`.swf`) and Director (`.dcr`)
material originally published on americangirl.com.

That material is the property of its respective rights holders. "American
Girl" is a trademark of Mattel, Inc. This project is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by Mattel or American Girl.

No copyright claim is made over any of it, and no license to it is granted
here. The MIT grant above covers only the original code. It is reproduced
as a non-commercial historical preservation of a website that no longer
exists in any usable form, of a version retired in a 2011 redesign, and is
distributed in that spirit and no other.

If you hold rights in this material and would like something removed,
please open an issue or contact the maintainer, and it will be taken down.


3. BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY RUNTIMES
--------------------------------

The distributed applications bundle software written by others, each under
its own terms:

  • Ruffle (https://ruffle.rs): MIT / Apache-2.0
  • Wine (https://winehq.org): LGPL-2.1-or-later
  • Adobe Flash Player projector and Adobe Director / Shockwave projector:
    proprietary Adobe software, both retired end-of-life products,
    redistributed here only as the runtime necessary to play the archived
    material. Not covered by the MIT grant above.

The projector binaries are deliberately NOT committed to this repository;
they are fetched at build time (see `tools/fetch-projector.sh`).
